            <section class="guide-summary" id="short-answer">
                <p class="guide-kicker">The short answer</p>
                <p>Happy Scale is a well-loved iOS tracker that smooths daily noise into a moving-average trend, and it earns its reputation. WeekScale is a different philosophy: fixed calendar weeks instead of a rolling trend, a one-time price instead of a subscription, and no account or cloud. If the second philosophy sounds like you, WeekScale is the alternative.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="prose-section" id="happy-scale-strengths">
                <h2>What Happy Scale does well</h2>
                <p>To be clear about this: Happy Scale does several things very well, and an honest comparison starts there.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Its smoothing trend genuinely takes the sting out of daily fluctuation.</li>
                    <li>Predictions, milestone goals, and a passcode are thoughtful, well-built features.</li>
                    <li>Apple Health import and export, plus iPhone&ndash;iPad sync, are convenient.</li>
                    <li>It is maintained by a small team with years of polish behind it.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>If those features matter to you, Happy Scale is a good choice, and you should keep using it. WeekScale does not claim to replace it for everyone.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="prose-section" id="weekscale-differences">
                <h2>Where WeekScale differs</h2>
                <p>WeekScale is not a clone of Happy Scale, and it does not try to be. It makes different choices on purpose:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Calendar weeks instead of a moving average.</strong> A finished week stays finished and can be compared fairly with another week. <a class="inline-link" href="/weekly-average-weight">Read the full argument.</a></li>
                    <li><strong>No subscription.</strong> WeekScale is a one-time purchase &mdash; $6 USD or &euro;5 EUR &mdash; with updates included and no recurring fee.</li>
                    <li><strong>No account and no cloud.</strong> Data lives in the app's private storage on your device. The Android app isn't even granted internet permission, and the iOS app makes no direct network requests.</li>
                    <li><strong>No goal weight and no predictions.</strong> WeekScale deliberately does not cheer for a number or predict your future weight. The only thing it rewards is a more complete week.</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="guide-principle">
                    <strong>The difference is philosophy, not quality.</strong>
                    <span>Happy Scale smooths your trend. WeekScale keeps your week &mdash; and your data &mdash; on your phone.</span>
                </div>
            </section>

